{"session_id":"svc-1779931906863330147","seq":0,"type":"session.start","ts":"2026-05-28T01:31:48.157544817Z","data":{"provider":"","model":"haiku","sticky":{"key_present":true,"assignment":"not_applicable","bonus":0},"utilization":{"observed_at":"0001-01-01T00:00:00Z"},"resolved_harness":"claude","harness_source":"auto_route","resolved_model":"haiku","work_dir":"/Users/erik/Projects/.ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-4d81d3f0-20260528T013133-8581f868","max_iterations":0,"prompt":"\u003cexecute-bead\u003e\n  \u003cinstructions\u003e\nYou are executing one bead in an isolated DDx execution worktree. The bead\u0026#39;s \u0026lt;description\u0026gt; and \u0026lt;acceptance\u0026gt; are the contract: every AC must be provably satisfied by a specific code, test, or file after your commit.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Step 0: size check\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Too big if any holds:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- More than ~6 ACs spanning unrelated subsystems.\u0026#xA;- AC mixes design, implementation, integration tests, and docs.\u0026#xA;- Description names multiple feature-sized pieces.\u0026#xA;- More than ~500 lines across ~5+ files in unrelated packages.\u0026#xA;- If the bead description exceeds 8000 bytes, use a split-first pass.\u0026#xA;- Auto-decomposition is capped at depth 2: root beads may split once, children once more; reject third-level splits with an explanation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;If too big, decompose:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;1. `ddx bead create` for each child (copy parent\u0026#39;s labels and spec-id).\u0026#xA;2. `ddx bead dep add \u0026lt;child-id\u0026gt; \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt;` to record edges.\u0026#xA;3. `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;4. Write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path with child IDs, then stop.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Decomposition alone is success. Do not mix it with implementation.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## How to work\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Read first. If the bead names files, specs, or prior beads, read them before editing — do not guess.\u0026#xA;- Cross-reference each AC to concrete evidence (test, file, function) before committing. If you cannot point at it, it is not done.\u0026#xA;- Run the project\u0026#39;s test and lint commands before committing. **Do not commit red code** — fix failures first.\u0026#xA;- Run git/index mutations sequentially; do not use parallel tool calls for `git add`, `git commit`, or other staging/commit commands.\u0026#xA;- Stage with `git add \u0026lt;specific-paths\u0026gt;`; never `git add -A` (the worktree may have unrelated WIP).\u0026#xA;- If `lefthook run pre-commit` depends on staged files, rerun it after staging the exact commit set. A `no-staged-files` run is not acceptance evidence.\u0026#xA;- Commit exactly once when green; conventional-commit subject ending with `[\u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;]`. Stop after the commit.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s scope.\u0026#xA;- Current-bead lifecycle is orchestrator-owned. Do not run `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --claim`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --status \u0026lt;status\u0026gt;`, `ddx bead update \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt; --unclaim`, or `ddx bead close \u0026lt;bead-id\u0026gt;`. Step 0 still allows `ddx bead create`, `ddx bead dep add`, and `ddx bead update \u0026lt;parent-id\u0026gt; --notes \u0026#39;decomposed into \u0026lt;child-ids\u0026gt;\u0026#39;`.\u0026#xA;- If you cannot finish, write `no_changes_rationale.txt` under the bead metadata `bundle` path before exiting. No commit or rationale ⇒ DDx records `no_evidence_produced`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## no_changes contract\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;The `no_changes_rationale.txt` file under the bead metadata `bundle` path must contain one of:\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- `verification_command: \u0026lt;cmd\u0026gt;` — repo cwd; exit 0 closes, nonzero rejects.\u0026#xA;- `status: open` + `reason: \u0026lt;retryable\u0026gt;` — open, smart retry.\u0026#xA;- `status: proposed` + `reason: \u0026lt;operator needed\u0026gt;` — operator lane.\u0026#xA;- `status: blocked` + `reason: \u0026lt;external blocker\u0026gt;` — blocked lane.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;No pseudo-statuses. Bare rationales and `status: needs_investigation` are rejected.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;For orchestrator decomposition, add `orchestrator_action: decompose` alongside `status: open`.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Reports\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;Reports go under the bead metadata `bundle` path in `.ddx/executions/`. **Never write reports to `/tmp` or outside the repo**. Use a named in-repo path when given; otherwise write `\u0026lt;short-name\u0026gt;.md` there. Commit it with the code.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Mode and overrides\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DDX_MODE=bead_execution: edit code/docs for bead AC. Only broad queue-steward default is overridden; tracker, merge-policy, verification, safety stay active. Bead description/AC override CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, and defaults.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Review gate\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- The review is a gate, not an escape hatch — meet every AC in this pass.\u0026#xA;- Address every BLOCKING `\u0026lt;review-findings\u0026gt;` item; do not declare `no_changes` with blocking findings open.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Constraints\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Work only inside this execution worktree.\u0026#xA;- Keep `.ddx/executions/` intact — DDx uses it as execution evidence.\u0026#xA;- **Never run `ddx init`** — the workspace is initialized.\u0026#xA;- Do not modify files outside the bead\u0026#39;s named scope.\u0026#xA;- Do not rewrite CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, or other instruction files unless the bead asks.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## Long-running matrix/benchmark beads\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;For expensive commands (benchmarks, load tests, validation \u0026gt; 60s per variant):\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;- Write a matrix plan before launching expensive commands: list required configs, output paths, completion criteria.\u0026#xA;- Do not re-run the same long-running command unless: (1) the command fingerprint changed (args/env/config), AND (2) you document why prior output is invalid and what changed.\u0026#xA;- If a long-running command times out or is incomplete, exit with `status: open` + retryable `reason` in `no_changes_rationale.txt`. Do not silently retry; let the orchestrator decide.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;## When the work is done\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;After the commit succeeds and every AC is verified, stop. Return control to the orchestrator.\n  \u003c/instructions\u003e\n  \u003cbead id=\"fizeau-4d81d3f0\"\u003e\n    \u003ctitle\u003ebench-pr-A1: harbor-runner Docker image + shell harness/task adapters + runtime-probe + CONTRACTs\u003c/title\u003e\n    \u003cdescription\u003e\nPROBLEM: The Go runner forces host Python by putting the repo root on Harbor\u0026#39;s PYTHONPATH so Harbor can import scripts.benchmark.harbor_adapters.*. We want the host to need only bash + Node + Docker. Harbor and its agent plugins must move into a container, and the matrix-side Python harness_adapters/ must be re-expressed as shell so the bash runner (A2/A3) can call them.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ROOT CAUSE: cmd/bench/matrix.go:1117-1129 prepends opts.repoRoot to PYTHONPATH so harbor_adapters resolve on the host; cmd/bench/matrix.go:1014-1026 (harborAgentArgs) hardwires --agent-import-path scripts.benchmark.harbor_adapters.\u0026lt;x\u0026gt;; the only harness IO contract today is Python under scripts/benchmark/harness_adapters/{fiz,opencode,pi,cost_probe,noop,dumb_script}.py with harbor classes at scripts/benchmark/harbor_agent.py:83 (FizeauAgent) and scripts/benchmark/harbor_adapters/{claude.py:31,codex.py:32,opencode.py:64,pi.py:68}.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;PROPOSED FIX:\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/Dockerfile.harbor-runner: FROM python:3.12-slim; pip install --no-cache-dir harbor-bench==\u0026lt;pinned\u0026gt; (5-min spike: confirm pip vs pip install git+https://github.com/laude-institute/...); COPY harbor_adapters/ and harbor_agent.py into /app; ENV PYTHONPATH=/app; WORKDIR /app; ENTRYPOINT [\u0026#34;harbor\u0026#34;].\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/build-harbor-runner.sh: docker build with --label image-content-sha=\u0026lt;sha256 of harbor_adapters/ + harbor_agent.py + Dockerfile.harbor-runner\u0026gt; (build-harbor-runner.sh:21-36 prototypes the hash); ./benchmark preflight rebuilds when cached label != current sha.\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/task-executors/harbor: bash wrapper; docker run --rm -v /var/run/docker.sock:/var/run/docker.sock -v \u0026#34;$cell_dir:/output\u0026#34; -v \u0026#34;$tasks_dir:/tasks:ro\u0026#34; -e FIZEAU_API_KEY -e FIZEAU_BASE_URL -e FIZEAU_MODEL fizeau-harbor-runner:latest run --agent-import-path \u0026#34;$harbor_plugin\u0026#34; --task-id \u0026#34;$task_id\u0026#34; --output /output; reads task-spec.json on stdin; writes cell_dir/result.json; records task_executor_version + harbor_runner_image_digest into \u0026lt;out\u0026gt;/sweep.json (runner copies into each cell).\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/harness-adapters/{fiz,claude,codex,opencode,pi,cost-probe,noop,dumb-script}: each executable with a \u0026#39;# SUMMARY:\u0026#39; header and two subcommands: install \u0026lt;agent-artifact-path\u0026gt; -\u0026gt; install-spec.json {install_command, artifact_source, binary_path, harbor_plugin}; command (profile JSON on stdin) -\u0026gt; command-spec.json {command, env, secret_env_keys}. claude/codex emit harbor_plugin scripts.benchmark.harbor_adapters.{claude:ClaudeAgent,codex:CodexAgent}; fiz emits scripts.benchmark.harbor_agent:FizeauAgent. Python harness_adapters/*.py are the reference for emitted shapes.\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/runtime-probe.sh: case on profile.metadata.runtime -\u0026gt; curl + jq each backend (lucebox, llamacpp, vllm, omlx, ds4, rapid-mlx, one arm each) -\u0026gt; model_server JSON {name,version,commit,endpoint}.\u0026#xA;- scripts/benchmark/{task-executors,harness-adapters}/CONTRACT.md document the JSON shapes and the \u0026#39;# SUMMARY:\u0026#39; convention.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;NON-SCOPE: runner dispatch/--plan/matrix expansion (A2); per-cell execution loop, resume/retry, report compose (A3); concurrency/signals/budget (A4); Go changes, deactivation, parity (A5); cell-report.schema.json (PR B); tasks_from/task_executor bench-set schema (PR C); Node collector (PR D); Node importers (PR E); deleting cmd/bench (PR F); docs (PR G).\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;DEPENDENCY: parent fizeau-163efede. Foundation bead — no sibling deps; A2/A3/A5 depend on this. Governing artifact: plan-2026-05-15-benchmark-runner-simplification.\u0026#xA;\u0026#xA;ACCEPTANCE:\u0026#xA;1. ./benchmark harness-adapters and ./benchmark task-executors list every adapter with its \u0026#39;# SUMMARY:\u0026#39; line. Test: Test_AdapterListing (scripts/benchmark/tests/adapters.bats).\u0026#xA;2. echo \u0026lt;profile.json\u0026gt; | harness-adapters/fiz command emits command-spec.json matching harness_adapters/fiz.py; harness-adapters/\u0026lt;x\u0026gt; install emits install-spec.json with the correct harbor_plugin for all 8. Test: Test_AdapterContract_fiz, Test_AdapterContract_claude, Test_AdapterContract_codex (adapters.bats); TestHarborAgentInstall (scripts/benchmark/test_harbor_agent.py).\u0026#xA;3. build-harbor-runner.sh builds fizeau-harbor-runner:latest with an image-content-sha label equal to sha256 of harbor_adapters/+harbor_agent.py+Dockerfile.harbor-runner; a re-run with no source change is a cache hit (label unchanged). Test: Test_BuildLabelMatchesContentSha (scripts/benchmark/tests/build_label.bats).\u0026#xA;4. runtime-probe.sh emits model_server JSON for each of the 6 backends from a captured fixture. Test: Test_RuntimeProbe_lucebox, Test_RuntimeProbe_vllm (scripts/benchmark/tests/runtime_probe.bats).\u0026#xA;Gates: go test ./... and lefthook run pre-commit both pass.\n    \u003c/description\u003e\n    \u003cacceptance\u003e\nAdapters/image/runtime-probe ACs 1-4 pass; go test ./... and lefthook run pre-commit green.\n    \u003c/acceptance\u003e\n    \u003clabels\u003earea:bench, kind:feature, governing:plan-2026-05-15-benchmark-runner-simplification, pr:A, triage:no-changes-unjustified\u003c/labels\u003e\n    \u003cmetadata parent=\"fizeau-11e9c095\" base-rev=\"ded5485ea477ac003d78cc5b4cdf0302026a18a1\" bundle=\".ddx/executions/20260528T013133-8581f868\"/\u003e\n  \u003c/bead\u003e\n  \u003cgoverning\u003e\n    \u003cnote\u003eNo governing references were pre-resolved. The bead description above is the primary contract. If it names files, specs, or prior beads, read them first. Ground decisions in repository state; do not guess.\u003c/note\u003e\n  \u003c/governing\u003e\n\u003c/execute-bead\u003e\n","metadata":{"DDX_MODE":"bead_execution","GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL":"/Users/erik/Projects/.ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-4d81d3f0-20260528T013133-8581f868/.ddx/executions/20260528T013133-8581f868/embedded/git-global.cfg","GIT_CONFIG_SYSTEM":"/dev/null","PATH":"/Users/erik/Projects/.ddx-exec-wt/.execute-bead-wt-fizeau-4d81d3f0-20260528T013133-8581f868/.ddx/executions/20260528T013133-8581f868/embedded/git-bin:/usr/local/cuda/bin:/home/erik/.jbang/bin:/home/erik/.opencode/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/installs/bun/1.3.11/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/installs/node/22.21.1/bin:/Users/erik/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/shims:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/home/erik/.local/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-subrepo/lib:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/Applications/SnowSQL.app/Contents/MacOS:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/Users/erik/.antigravity/antigravity/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.local/share/mise/shims:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/bin:/home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/sbin:/home/erik/.local/bin:/home/erik/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-subrepo/lib:/home/erik/.local/share/coursier/bin:/home/erik/.dotfiles/git-fuzzy/bin:/home/erik/go/bin